Q: Odoo 17.0 skip purchase_price recalculation on partner_id change A: <p>The double trigger of <code>_compute_purchase_price()</code> happens because Odoo's ORM recomputes stored computed fields whenever any of their <code>@api.depends</code> fields change — once during the <code>onchange</code> (when <code>partner_id</code> changes in the form) and again during <code>write()</code> when saving. This is expected ORM behavior in Odoo 17, but you can control it.</p>
<p><strong>Approach 1: Context flag to skip recomputation</strong></p>
<p>Override <code>_compute_purchase_price</code> and use a context key to skip the second computation:</p>
<p>python</p>
<pre><code>from odoo import api, models

class SaleOrderLine(models.Model):
    _inherit = 'sale.order.line'

    @api.depends('product_id', 'product_uom', 'company_id', 'currency_id', 'product_uom_qty')
    def _compute_purchase_price(self):
        if self.env.context.get('skip_purchase_price_recompute'):
            return
        return super()._compute_purchase_price()
</code></pre>
<p>Then override <code>write()</code> on <code>sale.order</code> to pass the flag when only <code>partner_id</code> is changing:</p>
<p>python</p>
<pre><code>class SaleOrder(models.Model):
    _inherit = 'sale.order'

    def write(self, vals):
        if 'partner_id' in vals and len(vals) == 1:
            return super().with_context(
                skip_purchase_price_recompute=True
            ).write(vals)
        return super().write(vals)
</code></pre>
<p><strong>Approach 2: Override and cache the value before partner change</strong></p>
<p>If you want to preserve the <code>purchase_price</code> value that was set <em>before</em> the partner change, store it and restore it after recomputation:</p>
<p>python</p>
<pre><code>class SaleOrderLine(models.Model):
    _inherit = 'sale.order.line'

    @api.depends('product_id', 'product_uom', 'company_id', 'currency_id', 'product_uom_qty')
    def _compute_purchase_price(self):
        # Cache existing values for lines that already have a purchase_price
        cached = {
            line.id: line.purchase_price 
            for line in self 
            if line.id and line.purchase_price
        }
        super()._compute_purchase_price()

        # Restore cached values if partner_id triggered this
        if self.env.context.get('from_partner_change'):
            for line in self:
                if line.id in cached:
                    line.purchase_price = cached[line.id]
</code></pre>
<p><strong>Approach 3 (simplest): Remove the dependency trigger</strong></p>
<p>If you don't need <code>purchase_price</code> to change based on partner at all, the cleanest solution is to remove <code>partner_id</code> from the dependency chain. Check if <code>_compute_purchase_price</code> in your Odoo 17 version depends on fields that chain through <code>order_id.partner_id</code>. If so, override it and narrow the <code>@api.depends</code>:</p>
<p>python</p>
<pre><code>class SaleOrderLine(models.Model):
    _inherit = 'sale.order.line'

    @api.depends('product_id', 'product_uom', 'company_id', 'currency_id')
    def _compute_purchase_price(self):
        return super()._compute_purchase_price()
</code></pre>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Note:</strong> Approach 3 means <code>purchase_price</code> won't auto-update when partner changes — which may be exactly what you want. But be aware that if your margin calculations depend on partner-specific costs/pricelists, you'd lose that auto-update.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'd recommend <strong>Approach 1</strong> — it's the safest because it only skips during partner-only writes and keeps all other recomputation behavior intact.</p>
